<title>USA: Base Ten Q3 loss $0.33 vs profit $0.01.</title>
<headline>Base Ten Q3 loss $0.33 vs profit $0.01.</headline>
<dateline>TRENTON, N.J. 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended</p>
<p>			July 31, 1996	July 31, 1995</p>
<p> Oper shr (loss)  $(0.33)		  0.01</p>
<p> Oper     (loss)  (2,505.0)		75.0</p>
<p> Revs		 3,032.0		  5,001.0</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted 7,565,040		7,511,023</p>
<p>			 9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Oper shr (loss)  $(1.04)		  $(0.13)</p>
<p> Oper net (loss)  (7,936.0)		(898.0)</p>
<p> Revs		 10,502.0		 13,135.0</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted 7,660,300		6,684,017</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers) NOTE: Third quarter 1995 revenues includes recognition of $1.05 million of royalties from sale of PRENVAL to Johnson &amp; Johnson Clinical Diagnostic Laboratories. The 1996 third quarter net loss includes a write-off of $569,000.</p>
<p>Third quarter 1996 results reflect a delay in receiving funding for Maintenance Data Recorder and the Interference Blanker Unit.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
